IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 9: Repeal and amendment of laws.
--
-- When a repeal takes effect (s 85) and when a law is automatically repealed (s 89 (1) to (6), (8)) are in `act-interpretation-time.l4`.
-- This module holds the rest of the chapter: the words amend, law and repeal (s 82), the effect of an Act amending a statutory instrument (s 83),
-- what repeal and amendment save (ss 84 to 88), the rest of s 89, and how amendments are made and read (ss 90 to 96).
-- The definitions inside these sections are also in `act-section-definitions.l4`.
--
-- Where a section says that something "does not" happen "only because" of a ground, the function answers JUST FALSE when the ground is the only one,
-- and NOTHING when it is not, because the text then says nothing.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 9, Repeal and amendment`

§§ `Part 9.1: General`

DECLARE `Kind of change to a law` IS ONE OF
    `an amendment`
    `a modification`
    `a repeal`
    `a lapse`
    `an expiry`
    `an omission and re-enactment in the same law`
    `an omission and re-enactment in another law`

-- src:1144 | amend includes modify.
@ref s 82, definition of amend (src:1144-1144)
GIVEN change IS A `Kind of change to a law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82: the change is an amendment for chapter 9` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `an amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a modification` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a repeal` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a lapse` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an expiry` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in the same law` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in another law` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1145 | law means an Act or statutory instrument.
@ref s 82, definition of law (src:1145-1145)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 82: the kind of document is a law for chapter 9` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN TRUE

-- src:1147 | repeal includes lapse and expire.
@ref s 82, definition of repeal (src:1147-1147)
GIVEN change IS A `Kind of change to a law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82: the change is a repeal for chapter 9` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `a repeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a lapse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an expiry` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an amendment` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a modification` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in the same law` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in another law` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1150 | (1) If an Act amends a statutory instrument, the instrument may be amended or repealed as if the amendment had been made by another statutory instrument of that kind.
@ref s 83 (1) (src:1150-1150)
GIVEN anActAmendsAStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 83 (1): the instrument may be amended or repealed as if the amendment had been made by another statutory instrument of that kind` MEANS anActAmendsAStatutoryInstrument

DECLARE `Thing a repeal or amendment may affect` IS ONE OF
    `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect (revival)`
    `the previous operation of the law, or anything done, begun or suffered under it`
    `an existing right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the law`
    `the proof of anything that has happened`
    `a right, privilege or liability saved by the law`
    `something else`

-- src:1155 | (1) The repeal or amendment of a law does not—
-- src:1156 | (a) revive anything not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect; or
-- src:1157 | (b) affect the previous operation of the law or anything done, begun or suffered under the law; or
-- src:1158 | (c) affect an existing right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the law.
-- src:1159 | (2) An investigation, proceeding or remedy in relation to an existing right, privilege or liability under the law may be started, exercised, continued or completed, and the right, privilege or liability may be enforced and any penalty imposed, as if the repeal or amendment had not happened.
-- src:1160 | (3) Without limiting subsections (1) and (2), the repeal or amendment of a law does not affect—
-- src:1161 | (a) the proof of anything that has happened; or
-- src:1162 | (b) any right, privilege or liability saved by the law.
@ref s 84 (1), (3) (src:1155-1162)
GIVEN thing IS A `Thing a repeal or amendment may affect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84 (1), (3): the repeal or amendment of a law affects the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `something not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect (revival)` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the previous operation of the law, or anything done, begun or suffered under it` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an existing right, privilege or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the law` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `the proof of anything that has happened` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a right, privilege or liability saved by the law` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1159 | (2) An investigation, proceeding or remedy in relation to an existing right, privilege or liability under the law may be started, exercised, continued or completed, and the right, privilege or liability may be enforced and any penalty imposed, as if the repeal or amendment had not happened.
@ref s 84 (2) (src:1159-1159)
GIVEN itIsInRelationToAnExistingRightPrivilegeOrLiabilityUnderTheLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84 (2): the investigation, proceeding or remedy may be started, exercised, continued or completed as if the repeal or amendment had not happened` MEANS
    IF   itIsInRelationToAnExistingRightPrivilegeOrLiabilityUnderTheLaw
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1163 | (4) This section does not limit any other provision of this chapter and is in addition to any provision of the law by which the repeal or amendment is made.
@ref s 84 (4) (src:1163-1163)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84 (4): s 84 limits any other provision of this chapter` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1173 | (1) If a law makes an act or omission an offence, the act or omission is only an offence if done or not done after the law commences.
@ref s 84A (1) (src:1173-1173)
GIVEN theLawMakesTheActOrOmissionAnOffence IS A BOOLEAN, dayOfTheActOrOmission IS A DATE, dayTheLawCommences IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 84A (1): the act or omission is an offence` MEANS
    IF   NOT (dayOfTheActOrOmission AT LEAST dayTheLawCommences)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF   theLawMakesTheActOrOmissionAnOffence
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1174 | (2) If a law increases the maximum or minimum penalty, or the penalty, for an offence, the increase applies only to an offence committed after the law commences.
@ref s 84A (2) (src:1174-1174)
GIVEN dayTheOffenceWasCommitted IS A DATE, dayTheLawCommences IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84A (2): the increase in the penalty applies to the offence` MEANS dayTheOffenceWasCommitted AT LEAST dayTheLawCommences

-- src:1175 | (3) If a law reduces the maximum or minimum penalty, or the penalty, for an offence, the reduction applies to an offence committed before or after the law commences, but does not affect any penalty imposed before the law commences.
@ref s 84A (3) (src:1175-1175)
GIVEN aPenaltyForTheOffenceWasImposedBeforeTheLawCommences IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84A (3): the reduction in the penalty applies to the offence` MEANS (NOT aPenaltyForTheOffenceWasImposedBeforeTheLawCommences)

-- src:1177 | law means an Act or subordinate law.
@ref s 84A (4), definition of law (src:1177-1177)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 84A (4): the kind of document is a law for s 84A` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

§§ `Part 9.2: Repeal`

-- src:1191 | (1) If a law (the first law) is repealed by another law (the other law), the first law is not revived only because the other law is repealed.
@ref s 86 (1) (src:1191-1191)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsThatTheOtherLawIsRepealed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 (1): the first law is revived` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsThatTheOtherLawIsRepealed
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1192 | (2) If a law (the first law) is amended by another law (the other law), the continuing operation of the amendments made by the other law is not affected only because the other law is repealed and, in particular, the first law is not revived in the form in which it was in before the amendments took effect only because of the repeal.
@ref s 86 (2) (src:1192-1192)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsThatTheOtherLawIsRepealed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 (2): the continuing operation of the amendments made by the other law is affected` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsThatTheOtherLawIsRepealed
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1193 | (3) This section does not limit any other provision of this chapter and is in addition to any provision of the law by which the repeal is made.
@ref s 86 (3) (src:1193-1193)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 86 (3): s 86 limits any other provision of this chapter` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1197 | amended does not include modified.
@ref s 86 (5), definition of amended (src:1197-1197)
GIVEN change IS A `Kind of change to a law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 (5): the change is an amendment for s 86` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `a modification` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an amendment` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a repeal` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a lapse` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an expiry` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in the same law` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in another law` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1198 | law includes a rule of the common law (including equity).
-- src:1199 | Examples
-- src:1200 | 1 a common law offence
-- src:1201 | 2 a common law rule of practice or procedure
-- src:1202 | 3 a right to equitable relief
@ref s 86 (5), definition of law (src:1198-1202)
GIVEN theThingIsARuleOfTheCommonLawIncludingEquity IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 (5): the thing is a law for s 86` MEANS
    IF   theThingIsARuleOfTheCommonLawIncludingEquity
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1199 | Examples
-- src:1200 | 1 a common law offence
-- src:1201 | 2 a common law rule of practice or procedure
-- src:1202 | 3 a right to equitable relief
@ref s 86 (5), examples (a rule of the common law) (src:1199-1202)
GIVEN example IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 (5), examples: the thing is a rule of the common law (including equity)` MEANS
    IF   elem example (LIST "a common law offence", "a common law rule of practice or procedure", "a right to equitable relief")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1205 | (1) If a provision of a law providing for the commencement of the law is repealed after the law has commenced, the repeal of the provision does not affect the continuing operation of the law.
@ref s 87 (1) (src:1205-1205)
GIVEN theLawHasCommenced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87 (1): the repeal of the provision providing for the commencement of the law affects the continuing operation of the law` MEANS
    IF   theLawHasCommenced
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1206 | (2) If a commencement notice providing for the commencement of a law is repealed after the law has commenced, the repeal of the notice does not affect the continuing operation of the law.
@ref s 87 (2) (src:1206-1206)
GIVEN theLawHasCommenced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 87 (2): the repeal of the commencement notice affects the continuing operation of the law` MEANS
    IF   theLawHasCommenced
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1207 | (3) This section does not limit any other provision of this chapter and is in addition to any provision of the law by which the repeal is made.
@ref s 87 (3) (src:1207-1207)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 87 (3): s 87 limits any other provision of this chapter` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1212 | (1) The continuing operation of a transitional law or validating law is not affected only because the law is repealed.
-- src:1213 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a law that is a transitional law or validating law because of modifications that it makes to another law.
@ref s 88 (1), (2) (src:1212-1213)
GIVEN theLawIsATransitionalLawOrValidatingLaw IS A BOOLEAN, onlyBecauseOfModificationsItMakesToAnotherLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theOnlyGroundIsThatTheLawIsRepealed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 (1), (2): the continuing operation of the law is affected` MEANS
    IF   theLawIsATransitionalLawOrValidatingLaw AND (NOT onlyBecauseOfModificationsItMakesToAnotherLaw) AND theOnlyGroundIsThatTheLawIsRepealed
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1214 | (3) If a law (the savings law) declares a law (the declared law) to be a law to which this section applies—
-- src:1215 | (a) the effect of the declared law does not end only because of its repeal; and
-- src:1216 | (b) the effect of the savings law does not end only because of its repeal.
@ref s 88 (3) (src:1214-1216)
GIVEN theSavingsLawDeclaresTheDeclaredLawToBeALawToWhichS88Applies IS A BOOLEAN, theOnlyGroundIsThatTheLawIsRepealed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 (3): the effect of the declared law or the savings law ends` MEANS
    IF   theSavingsLawDeclaresTheDeclaredLawToBeALawToWhichS88Applies AND theOnlyGroundIsThatTheLawIsRepealed
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1217 | (4) A declaration may be made for subsection (3) about a law whether or not the Act is a law to which subsection (1) applies.
@ref s 88 (4) (src:1217-1217)
GIVEN theActIsALawToWhichSubsection1Applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88 (4): a declaration may be made for subsection (3) about the law` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1218 | (5) A declaration made for subsection (3) about a law does not imply that, in the absence of a declaration about it, another law is not a law to which this section applies.
@ref s 88 (5) (src:1218-1218)
GIVEN aDeclarationWasMadeAboutAnotherLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88 (5): the declaration implies that, without a declaration about it, another law is not a law to which s 88 applies` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1219 | (6) This section does not limit any other provision of this chapter and is in addition to any provision of the law by which the repeal is made.
@ref s 88 (6) (src:1219-1219)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88 (6): s 88 limits any other provision of this chapter` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1222 | (8) To remove any doubt and without limiting section 6 (Legislation Act provisions must be applied), the application of this section to a law is not displaced only because the law is repealed and, in particular, the repeal of the law does not of itself imply an intention to displace the application of this section to the law.
@ref s 88 (8) (src:1222-1222)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsThatTheLawIsRepealed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88 (8): the application of s 88 to the law is displaced` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsThatTheLawIsRepealed
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1224 | transitional law means—
-- src:1225 | (a) a law made or expressed to be made for a transitional purpose; or
-- src:1226 | (b) a law that makes provision consequential on a law mentioned in paragraph (a).
-- src:1227 | Examples
-- src:1228 | 1 a provision stating that an existing licence under a repealed Act is taken to be a licence of a particular kind under another Act and authorising the imposition of conditions under the other Act
-- src:1229 | 2 a provision stating that a provision applies to certain applications made before the commencement of an amendment or only to applications made after the commencement of an amendment
-- src:1230 | 3 a declaration made for s (3)
-- src:1231 | Note Transitional is defined in the dictionary to include application and savings.
@ref s 88 (9), definition of transitional law (src:1224-1231)
GIVEN madeOrExpressedToBeMadeForATransitionalPurpose IS A BOOLEAN, makesProvisionConsequentialOnSuchALaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88 (9): the law is a transitional law` MEANS madeOrExpressedToBeMadeForATransitionalPurpose OR makesProvisionConsequentialOnSuchALaw

-- src:1232 | validating law means—
-- src:1233 | (a) a law that validates something that is or may be invalid; or
-- src:1234 | (b) a law that makes provision consequential on a law mentioned in paragraph (a).
-- src:1235 | Examples
-- src:1236 | 1 a provision declaring an instrument to have been validly made and acts done in reliance on the instrument to have been validly done
-- src:1237 | 2 a provision stating that an instrument that is declared valid is taken to have been amended in a particular way
@ref s 88 (9), definition of validating law (src:1232-1237)
GIVEN validatesSomethingThatIsOrMayBeInvalid IS A BOOLEAN, makesProvisionConsequentialOnSuchALaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 88 (9): the law is a validating law` MEANS validatesSomethingThatIsOrMayBeInvalid OR makesProvisionConsequentialOnSuchALaw

-- src:1252 | (7) A repeal under this section has effect for all purposes, including, for example, any other provisions of this chapter about repeals.
@ref s 89 (7) (src:1252-1252)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89 (7): a repeal under s 89 has effect for all purposes, including the provisions of this chapter about repeals` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1254 | (9) In the application of subsection (8) to a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, a reference to the instrument’s notification day is a reference to the day after the day it is made or, if it is required under an Act or statutory instrument to be approved (however described) by the Executive, a Minister or any other entity, the day after the day it is approved.
@ref s 89 (9) (src:1254-1254)
GIVEN `day made` IS A DATE, `day approved, if approval is required` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 89 (9): the notification day of a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, for s 89 (8)` MEANS
    `s 73 (4) (a): the day a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument is made or approved` `day made` `day approved, if approval is required`

-- src:1255 | (10) This section does not limit any other provision of this chapter.
@ref s 89 (10) (src:1255-1255)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89 (10): s 89 limits any other provision of this chapter` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1259 | amend does not include modify.
@ref s 89 (12), definition of amend (src:1259-1259)
GIVEN change IS A `Kind of change to a law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 89 (12): the change is an amendment for s 89` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `a modification` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an amendment` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a repeal` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a lapse` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an expiry` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in the same law` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in another law` THEN NOTHING

-- s 89 (12): an amending law consists only of provisions of the kinds listed in (a) to (j).
DECLARE `Kind of provision in a law` IS ONE OF
    `the Act's long title`
    `a preamble or recital`
    `a provision about the law's name`
    `a provision about the law's commencement`
    `a provision about the purposes of the law or any of its provisions`
    `a provision about the effect of notes`
    `a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of a law (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed law)`
    `a provision declaring a law to be a law to which section 88 applies`
    `a provision about the renumbering of a law`
    `a provision authorising or requiring something to be done under chapter 11`
    `a provision of any other kind`

-- src:1260 | amending law means a law that consists only of provisions of the following kinds:
-- src:1261 | (a) for an Act—the Act’s long title;
-- src:1262 | (b) a preamble or recital (however described);
-- src:1263 | (c) a provision about the law’s name;
-- src:1264 | (d) a provision about the law’s commencement;
-- src:1265 | (e) a provision about the purposes of the law or any of its provisions;
-- src:1266 | (f) a provision about the effect of notes;
-- src:1267 | Note A note itself is not part of an Act or statutory instrument (see s 127).
-- src:1268 | (g) a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of a law (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed law);
-- src:1269 | (h) a provision declaring a law to be a law to which section 88 (Repeal does not end effect of transitional laws etc) applies;
-- src:1270 | (i) a provision about the renumbering of a law;
-- src:1271 | (j) a provision authorising or requiring something to be done under chapter 11 (Republication of Acts and statutory instruments).
@ref s 89 (12), definition of amending law (src:1260-1271)
GIVEN theLawIsAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, provisions IS A LIST OF `Kind of provision in a law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89 (12): the law is an amending law` MEANS
    `all the provisions are of the listed kinds` theLawIsAnAct provisions

GIVEN theLawIsAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, provisions IS A LIST OF `Kind of provision in a law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`all the provisions are of the listed kinds` MEANS
    CONSIDER provisions
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `the provision is of a listed kind` theLawIsAnAct first AND `all the provisions are of the listed kinds` theLawIsAnAct rest

GIVEN theLawIsAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, kind IS A `Kind of provision in a law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the provision is of a listed kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the Act's long title` THEN theLawIsAnAct
    WHEN `a preamble or recital` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision about the law's name` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision about the law's commencement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision about the purposes of the law or any of its provisions` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision about the effect of notes` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision providing for the amendment or repeal of a law (including a provision identifying the amended or repealed law)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision declaring a law to be a law to which section 88 applies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision about the renumbering of a law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision authorising or requiring something to be done under chapter 11` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a provision of any other kind` THEN FALSE

-- src:1272 | amending provision, of a law, means a provision of the law that only amends or repeals a law, and includes—
-- src:1273 | (a) any other provision (for example, a schedule) of the law that only identifies the law amended or repealed; and
-- src:1274 | (b) any other provision (for example, a part heading) of the law that only identifies (or groups) provisions that are amended or repealed.
@ref s 89 (12), definition of amending provision (src:1272-1274)
GIVEN onlyAmendsOrRepealsALaw IS A BOOLEAN, onlyIdentifiesTheLawAmendedOrRepealed IS A BOOLEAN, onlyIdentifiesOrGroupsProvisionsThatAreAmendedOrRepealed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89 (12): the provision is an amending provision` MEANS
    onlyAmendsOrRepealsALaw OR onlyIdentifiesTheLawAmendedOrRepealed OR onlyIdentifiesOrGroupsProvisionsThatAreAmendedOrRepealed

-- src:1276 | commencement provision, of a law, means a provision of the law that only provides for the commencement of the law.
@ref s 89 (12), definition of commencement provision (src:1276-1276)
GIVEN onlyProvidesForTheCommencementOfTheLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 89 (12): the provision is a commencement provision` MEANS onlyProvidesForTheCommencementOfTheLaw

§§ `Part 9.3: Amendment`

-- src:1281 | A law and all laws amending it are to be read as one.
@ref s 90 (src:1281-1281)
GIVEN aLawAndAllLawsAmendingIt IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 90: the law and all laws amending it are to be read as one` MEANS aLawAndAllLawsAmendingIt

DECLARE `Kind of inserted provision` IS ONE OF
    `an inserted chapter, part, division, subdivision, section or subsection`
    `an inserted paragraph`
    `an inserted subparagraph`
    `an inserted sub-subparagraph`
    `an inserted definition`
    `a miscellaneous inserted provision`

DECLARE `Position where a provision is inserted` IS ONE OF
    `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
    `the appropriate alphabetical position`
    `the appropriate alphabetical position, worked out on a letter-by-letter basis, in a series of definitions`
    `the appropriate position`

-- src:1284 | (1) This section applies if a law (the amending law) amends another law (the amended law) by inserting any of the following provisions, and does not exactly specify the position in the amended law where it is to be inserted:
-- src:1285 | (a) a chapter, part, division, subdivision, section or subsection (an inserted chapter, part, division, subdivision, section or subsection);
-- src:1286 | (b) a paragraph (an inserted paragraph);
-- src:1287 | (c) a subparagraph (an inserted subparagraph);
-- src:1288 | (d) a sub-subparagraph (an inserted sub-subparagraph);
-- src:1289 | (e) a definition (an inserted definition);
-- src:1290 | (f) any other provision (a miscellaneous inserted provision).
@ref s 91 (1) (src:1284-1290)
GIVEN aLawAmendsAnotherLawByInsertingAProvision IS A BOOLEAN, itDoesNotExactlySpecifyThePosition IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91 (1): s 91 applies to the amendment` MEANS aLawAmendsAnotherLawByInsertingAProvision AND itDoesNotExactlySpecifyThePosition

-- src:1291 | (2) An inserted chapter, part, division, subdivision, section or subsection is inserted in the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position in the amended law.
-- src:1292 | (3) An inserted paragraph is inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position in the amended law.
-- src:1293 | (4) An inserted subparagraph is inserted in the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position in the amended law.
-- src:1294 | (5) An inserted sub-subparagraph is inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position in the amended law.
-- src:1295 | (6) An inserted definition is inserted in the appropriate alphabetical position (worked out on a letter-by-letter basis) in a series of definitions in the amended law.
-- src:1296 | (7) A miscellaneous inserted provision is inserted in the appropriate position in the amended law.
@ref s 91 (2) to (7) (src:1291-1296)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of inserted provision`
GIVETH A `Position where a provision is inserted`
`s 91 (2) to (7): the position of the inserted provision in the amended law` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an inserted chapter, part, division, subdivision, section or subsection` THEN `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
    WHEN `an inserted paragraph` THEN `the appropriate alphabetical position`
    WHEN `an inserted subparagraph` THEN `the appropriate numerical or alphanumerical position`
    WHEN `an inserted sub-subparagraph` THEN `the appropriate alphabetical position`
    WHEN `an inserted definition` THEN `the appropriate alphabetical position, worked out on a letter-by-letter basis, in a series of definitions`
    WHEN `a miscellaneous inserted provision` THEN `the appropriate position`

-- src:1297 | (8) In applying this section to a law that is divided otherwise than into sections, a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law.
@ref s 91 (8) (src:1297-1297)
GIVEN theLawIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 91 (8): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law` MEANS theLawIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections

-- s 91 (9): the matters to which regard may be had in working out the appropriate position (copied from the text, one string per paragraph).
-- src:1298 | (9) In working out the appropriate position where a provision is to be inserted in the amended law, regard may be had to the following:
-- src:1299 | (a) the provision number or letter;
-- src:1300 | (b) the heading of the relevant amending provision of the amending law;
-- src:1301 | (c) any other amendments in the amending law including the order of amendments;
-- src:1302 | (d) anything else in the amending law or amended law;
-- src:1303 | (e) current legislative drafting practice.
@ref s 91 (9) (src:1298-1303)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 91 (9): the matters to which regard may be had in working out the appropriate position` MEANS
    LIST
        "(a) the provision number or letter;"
        , "(b) the heading of the relevant amending provision of the amending law;"
        , "(c) any other amendments in the amending law including the order of amendments;"
        , "(d) anything else in the amending law or amended law;"
        , "(e) current legislative drafting practice."

-- src:1307 | insert includes relocate.
@ref s 91 (11), definition of insert (src:1307-1307)
GIVEN theThingIsARelocation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91 (11): the thing is an insertion` MEANS
    IF   theThingIsARelocation
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of word amendment` IS ONE OF
    `omitting a word`
    `substituting a word for another word`
    `inserting a word before or after a particular word`
    `another kind of amendment`

-- src:1310 | (1) If a law amends another law—
-- src:1311 | (a) by omitting a word; or
-- src:1312 | (b) by substituting a word for another word; or
-- src:1313 | (c) by inserting a word before or after a particular word;
-- src:1314 | the amendment is to be made wherever possible in the other law.
@ref s 92 (1) (src:1310-1314)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of word amendment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 92 (1): the amendment is to be made wherever possible in the other law` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `omitting a word` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `substituting a word for another word` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `inserting a word before or after a particular word` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another kind of amendment` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `Material belonging to a provision for amendment purposes` IS ONE OF
    `a heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, dictionary, section or any other provision`
    `an example at the end of a provision`
    `a note at the end of a provision`
    `a penalty at the end of a subsection`
    `a penalty at the end of a section that is not divided into subsections`
    `the word and, or or but, or a similar word, at the end of a paragraph or other provision`

DECLARE `What the material is part of` IS ONE OF
    `part of the provision it belongs to`
    `not part of that provision`
    `part of the section`

-- src:1319 | (1) This section applies for the purpose of amending a law.
-- src:1320 | (2) The heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, dictionary, section or any other provision of the law forms part of the provision to which it is a heading.
-- src:1321 | (3) An example at the end of a provision of the law is part of the provision unless the example is expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to another provision.
-- src:1322 | (4) A note at the end of a provision of the law is taken, for this section, to be part of the provision unless the note is expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to another provision.
-- src:1323 | (5) However, a note in a law is not, for any other purpose, part of the law.
-- src:1324 | Note Section 127 (Material that is not part of Act or statutory instrument) deals with the status of notes.
-- src:1325 | (6) A penalty at the end of a subsection of the law—
-- src:1326 | (a) is part of the subsection unless the penalty is expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to other subsections of the section; or
-- src:1327 | (b) if the penalty is expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to other subsections—is part of the section.
-- src:1328 | (7) A penalty at the end of a section of the law that is not divided into subsections is part of the section.
-- src:1329 | (8) The word ‘and’, ‘or’ or ‘but’, or a similar word, at the end of a paragraph, subparagraph, sub-subparagraph or another provision of the law is part of the provision.
@ref s 93 (1) to (8) (src:1319-1329)
GIVEN material IS A `Material belonging to a provision for amendment purposes`, expressedToApplyOnlyToAnotherProvision IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What the material is part of`
`s 93 (2) to (8): what the material is part of, for the purpose of amending a law` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
    WHEN `a heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, dictionary, section or any other provision` THEN `part of the provision it belongs to`
    WHEN `an example at the end of a provision` THEN
        IF   expressedToApplyOnlyToAnotherProvision
        THEN `not part of that provision`
        ELSE `part of the provision it belongs to`
    WHEN `a note at the end of a provision` THEN
        IF   expressedToApplyOnlyToAnotherProvision
        THEN `not part of that provision`
        ELSE `part of the provision it belongs to`
    WHEN `a penalty at the end of a subsection` THEN
        IF   expressedToApplyOnlyToAnotherProvision
        THEN `part of the section`
        ELSE `part of the provision it belongs to`
    WHEN `a penalty at the end of a section that is not divided into subsections` THEN `part of the provision it belongs to`
    WHEN `the word and, or or but, or a similar word, at the end of a paragraph or other provision` THEN `part of the provision it belongs to`

-- src:1323 | (5) However, a note in a law is not, for any other purpose, part of the law.
@ref s 93 (5) (src:1323-1323)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 93 (5): a note in a law is, for any other purpose, part of the law` MEANS FALSE

DECLARE `Material at the end of a provision` IS ONE OF
    `an example`
    `a note`
    `a penalty`

-- src:1330 | (9) In working out whether an example or note is at the end of a provision of the law, any penalty is to be disregarded, and, for an example, any note is to be disregarded.
-- src:1331 | Note According to current legislative drafting practice, examples, notes and penalties to a provision are arranged in the following order at the end of provisions:
-- src:1332 | 1 penalty (first)
-- src:1333 | 2 examples
-- src:1334 | 3 notes (last).
@ref s 93 (9) (src:1330-1334)
GIVEN material IS A `Material at the end of a provision`, thing IS A `Material at the end of a provision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 93 (9): the thing is disregarded in working out whether the material is at the end of the provision` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
    WHEN `a penalty` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a note` THEN
        IF   thing EQUALS `a penalty`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `an example` THEN
        IF   thing EQUALS `a penalty` OR thing EQUALS `a note`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1335 | (10) In applying this section to a law that is divided otherwise than into sections, a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law.
@ref s 93 (10) (src:1335-1335)
GIVEN theLawIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 93 (10): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the law` MEANS theLawIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections

-- src:1340 | (1) This section applies if—
-- src:1341 | (a) a law expressly or impliedly authorises or requires—
-- src:1342 | (i) the making of an appointment or statutory instrument; or
-- src:1343 | (ii) the delegation of a function; or
-- src:1344 | (iii) the issue of a licence or permit (however described); or
-- src:1345 | (iv) the doing (however described) of anything else; and
-- src:1346 | (b) the law is amended by another law; and
-- src:1347 | (c) under the amended law—
-- src:1348 | (i) the appointment or statutory instrument may be made; or
-- src:1349 | (ii) the function may be delegated; or
-- src:1350 | (iii) the licence or permit may be issued; or
-- src:1351 | (iv) the thing may be done;
-- src:1352 | whether by the same or a different entity.
@ref s 94 (1) (src:1340-1352)
GIVEN aLawAuthorisesOrRequiresTheMakingOfAnAppointmentOrInstrumentADelegationALicenceOrPermitOrAnythingElse IS A BOOLEAN, theLawIsAmendedByAnotherLaw IS A BOOLEAN, underTheAmendedLawTheThingMayStillBeDone IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 94 (1): s 94 applies to the appointment, instrument, delegation, licence, permit or other thing` MEANS
    aLawAuthorisesOrRequiresTheMakingOfAnAppointmentOrInstrumentADelegationALicenceOrPermitOrAnythingElse AND theLawIsAmendedByAnotherLaw AND underTheAmendedLawTheThingMayStillBeDone

-- src:1353 | Examples—par (a) (iv)
-- src:1354 | 1 the giving of an approval, consent or permission
-- src:1355 | 2 the making of a recommendation
@ref s 94 (1), examples (par (a) (iv)) (src:1353-1355)
GIVEN thing IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94 (1), examples: the thing is the doing of anything else, under par (a) (iv)` MEANS
    IF   elem thing (LIST "the giving of an approval, consent or permission", "the making of a recommendation")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1356 | (2) An appointment, statutory instrument, delegation, licence, permit or anything else mentioned in subsection (1) that was in force immediately before the commencement of the amendment continues to have effect as if it had been made, issued or done (however described) under the amended law.
@ref s 94 (2) (src:1356-1356)
GIVEN s94Applies IS A BOOLEAN, wasInForceImmediatelyBeforeTheCommencementOfTheAmendment IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94 (2): the thing continues to have effect as if it had been made, issued or done under the amended law` MEANS
    IF   s94Applies AND wasInForceImmediatelyBeforeTheCommencementOfTheAmendment
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1360 | amend includes omit and re-enact in the same law (with or without changes), but does not include omit and re-enact in another law.
@ref s 94 (4), definition of amend (src:1360-1360)
GIVEN change IS A `Kind of change to a law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 94 (4): the change is an amendment for s 94` MEANS
    CONSIDER change
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in the same law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an omission and re-enactment in another law` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an amendment` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a modification` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a repeal` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a lapse` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `an expiry` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1364 | (1) If a law is modified by another law, the law operates as modified but the modification does not amend the text of the law.
@ref s 95 (1) (src:1364-1364)
GIVEN theLawIsModifiedByAnotherLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 95 (1): the law operates as modified` MEANS theLawIsModifiedByAnotherLaw

-- src:1364 | (1) If a law is modified by another law, the law operates as modified but the modification does not amend the text of the law.
@ref s 95 (1) (src:1364-1364)
GIVEN theLawIsModifiedByAnotherLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95 (1): the modification amends the text of the law` MEANS
    IF   theLawIsModifiedByAnotherLaw
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1369 | (1) This section applies if a provision of a law is relocated (with or without changes) to a different place in the same law or to a different law.
@ref s 96 (1) (src:1369-1369)
GIVEN aProvisionIsRelocatedToADifferentPlaceInTheSameLawOrToADifferentLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 96 (1): s 96 applies to the provision` MEANS aProvisionIsRelocatedToADifferentPlaceInTheSameLawOrToADifferentLaw

-- src:1370 | (2) The operation or meaning of the provision is not affected only because of the provision’s relocation.
@ref s 96 (2) (src:1370-1370)
GIVEN theOnlyGroundIsTheProvisionsRelocation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96 (2): the operation or meaning of the provision is affected` MEANS
    IF   theOnlyGroundIsTheProvisionsRelocation
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1371 | (3) Without limiting subsection (2), if before its relocation the provision was to be interpreted in a particular way, it is to be interpreted in that way in its new location.
@ref s 96 (3) (src:1371-1371)
GIVEN beforeItsRelocationTheProvisionWasToBeInterpretedInAParticularWay IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96 (3): the provision is to be interpreted in that way in its new location` MEANS
    IF   beforeItsRelocationTheProvisionWasToBeInterpretedInAParticularWay
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1372 | (4) However, the provision has effect subject to any changes made to, or in relation to, it.
@ref s 96 (4) (src:1372-1372)
GIVEN changesAreMadeToOrInRelationToTheProvision IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 96 (4): the provision has effect subject to the changes` MEANS changesAreMadeToOrInRelationToTheProvision
